    "result_text": "The only test files are the acceptance suite (`AcceptanceTest`, `AcceptanceBase`, and one other helper). The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same first and last name, case-insensitively \u2014 on `POST /api/owners`, persisted and returned via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `Integer namesakeCount` field (`namesake_count` column) with getter/setter, alongside the existing `customerCode`.\n- **New `function/owner/CountNamesakes.java`** \u2014 an OfficeFloor step that counts owners in the repository matching the new owner's first+last name via `equalsIgnoreCase`, and stores the result on the owner. It runs *before* `SaveOwner`, so the owner being created is not counted (matching the \"before this create\" semantics, same pattern as `AssignCustomerCode`).\n- **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `namesakes` step into the pipeline between `customerCode` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n- **Schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column; also appended a trailing `NULL` to the positional owner `INSERT`s in `hsqldb/data.sql` to match the new column count.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCountsNamesakes` passes and the full suite builds green.",
